2026-11-06T02:57:37.7861284Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7869728Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7870544Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7871023Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7871262Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7871451Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7871787Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7872086Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7872522Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7872738Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7872931Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7873254Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7873466Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7873688Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7874251Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T02:57:37.7874431Z 
